# Node roster: maps each node's RADIO MAC to its name and IPv4 host octet.
# Manually managed; add one line per node. Two consumers, both driven off this
# one table:
#
#   batctl    prints names instead of hex in `batctl o` / `batctl n`.
#             Cosmetic only -- gives no IP-level reachability.
#   installer derives every node's mesh address from its MAC (EUI-64 against
#             the shared ULA prefix) and writes <name>.mesh entries into
#             /etc/hosts, and sets this node's hostname, which is what makes
#             <name>.local resolvable over mDNS. The v4 octet below gives the
#             node's address on the router's LAN.
#
# Bare names, no domain suffix. The name is used verbatim as the system
# hostname, so a suffix here becomes part of the hostname and then part of
# every name derived from it.
#
# The v4 octet is an EXPLICIT column, not derived. It used to come from a
# node's line POSITION in this file, which meant inserting a node anywhere but
# the end silently renumbered every node below it -- every one of them then
# needed a fleet-wide reinstall to pick up its new address, over a change that
# was supposed to touch only the node being added. Writing the octet down
# fixes a node's address to its NAME instead of its position, so the roster
# can grow anywhere without moving anyone else.
#
# The value must be greater than 1 (below that is the router itself) and less
# than 100 (where dnsmasq's laptop pool starts), and unique across this file --
# nothing here checks for a typo'd duplicate, and two nodes sharing an octet
# is a silent address collision in the field.
#
# heylo-base's octet (14) is nominal: heylo-base is the OpenWrt router, it
# never runs install_network_stack.sh, and its real LAN address is
# 192.168.12.1, set via UCI (see docs/OPENWRT.md). It carries a column entry
# only to keep this table uniform.
#
# Format:  <radio-mac>            <name>          <v4-octet>
# ------------------------------------------------------------
0c:bf:74:00:5b:c8    olo            11
0c:bf:74:00:57:4a    drone          12
0c:bf:74:00:5e:19    ragnarhorn     13
0c:bf:74:00:37:57    heylo-base     14
